  "body": "Fixes #7043\n\n## What to review first\n1. `lib/server.js`: the `{ server, closePromise }` binding shape and `closeSecondary` resolving the promise (this is the root cause fix).\n2. `fastify.js` close block: `done()` now gates on `Promise.all` of secondary close promises.\n3. `test/close.test.js`: the regression test (request in-flight on the IPv4 secondary listener when `close()` is called).\n\n## Summary\n`fastify.close()` now waits for in-flight requests on ALL dual-stack listeners (main + secondary) before resolving and running `onClose` hooks. Previously the secondary server's close callback was discarded (`close(() => {})`), so its drain was never awaited and `onClose` could release resources while a handler was still running.\n\n## Changes\n| File | Change |\n|---|---|\n| `lib/server.js` | Store `{ server, closePromise }` per binding; resolve the promise in the secondary close callback |\n| `fastify.js` | Gate `done()` on `Promise.all` of secondary close promises; adapt `addresses()` to the new binding shape |\n| `test/close.test.js` | Regression test for the secondary-listener drain path |\n\n## Verification\n- [x] `npm run unit`: full suite passes (2342 tests, 0 failures)\n- [x] `npm run lint`: clean\n- [x] `npm run coverage:ci-check-coverage`: 100% line coverage\n- [x] Repro: request a slow handler via the IPv4 secondary listener, call `close()` mid-request; `close()` waits (~1500ms), `onClose` fires with `inFlight = 0`\n\n## Out of scope\n- Single-bind (non-dual-stack) behavior is unchanged: `Promise.all([])` resolves immediately.\n- `forceCloseConnections` behavior is untouched.",
